<title>UK: UK intervention board details EU sugar sales.</title>
<headline>UK intervention board details EU sugar sales.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>A total 69,000 tonnes of current series white sugar received export rebates of a maximum 41.846 European Currency Units (Ecus) per 100 kilos at Wednesday's European Union (EU) tender, the U.K. Intervention Board said. Out of this, traders in France received 35,500 tonnes, in Denmark 5,000 tonnes, in Germany 13,000 and in the UK 15,500, it added. This week's award brings the cumulative tonnage awarded for export from the 1996/97 crop to 2.418 million tonnes. This compares with the 1,250 tonnes awarded on July 10, 1996, when the cumulative tonnage totalled 2.504 million tonnes.</p>
<p>--Christopher Lyddon, London newsroom +44 171 542 7928</p>
